1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,420
An island off Africa speaks
a language from Borneo.

2
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:07,400
This is Madagascar,
known as the Great Red Island.

3
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:10,520
Borneo sits on the far
side of the Indian Ocean.

4
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:12,360
Nobody is sure how this happened.

5
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:16,021
Today: who sailed here,
animals found nowhere else,

6
00:00:16,041 --> 00:00:18,390
and what never to do when you visit.

7
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,450
But first, the strangest clue.

8
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:24,590
Malagasy, the national language,
belongs to the Southeast Barito family.

9
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:27,680
Its closest relative is Maanyan,
spoken in Borneo.

10
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:31,500
Yet Madagascar sits only
400 kilometers from Africa.

11
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:35,090
Here is the twist:
the Maanyan were not seafarers.

12
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:38,230
Researchers think Malay sailors
may have carried them across.

13
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:41,060
The voyage likely happened
around the 7th or 8th century.

14
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:45,130
Genetic studies agree: Malagasy
people share more DNA with Borneo.

15
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:47,120
And that is only half of the mystery.

16
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:50,920
Madagascar split from Africa
135 million years ago.

17
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:53,770
Then it broke away from India,
88 million years ago.

18
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:56,110
Left alone, life went its own way.

19
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,320
98% of its mammals, reptiles
and amphibians exist nowhere else.

20
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:02,560
So do more than 90% of its plants.

21
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:05,660
Stay with me. The strangest
creature is still coming.

22
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:08,790
6 of the world's 8 baobab
species grow only here.

23
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:12,010
At sunset, the Avenue
of the Baobabs glows orange.

24
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,570
There are more than 100 species of lemurs.

25
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:26,070
98% of them are threatened
with extinction.

26
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:29,660
The indri sings so loudly
that it carries 2 kilometers.

27
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:32,660
Locals call it babakoto, meaning ancestor.

28
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:34,970
Madagascar once had giants.

29
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:37,820
Elephant birds stood about 3 meters tall.

30
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:40,520
Their eggs were 8 times
bigger than an ostrich's.

31
00:01:40,910 --> 00:01:44,310
One study claims bones with cut
marks over 10,000 years old.

32
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,310
If true, humans arrived far
earlier than we thought.

33
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:51,710
These birds vanished between 1,200
and 700 years ago, as livestock spread.

34
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:54,710
In 1896, France annexed the island.

35
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:57,550
Independence came on June 26th, 1960.

36
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,450
One last thing before you go: fady.

37
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:03,830
Fady are taboos, and they
change from village to village.

38
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:09,530
Ask locals: Inona no fady eto?
It means, what is forbidden here?

39
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:13,800
That was Madagascar. Which country should
we visit next? Tell me in the comments.
